//@version=6
// Box Finder – Accumulation / Distribution / Consolidation   ·   v1.6
// Changelog
//  v1.6  Squeeze Play on a higher timeframe too: its box on the chart, and a table of how often the chart's squeeze fires before the big one
//  v1.5  Second way to detect a box: "Squeeze Play" (Bollinger Bands inside the Keltner Channel); a "Squeeze Fired" panel when it ends
//  v1.4  Labels sit directly under the box they describe
//  v1.3  Table: how many head fakes still reached the ORIGINAL target (before the opposite one)
//  v1.2  Narrower table (the long footnote moved into a hover tooltip)
//  v1.1  Head fakes: when a break fails (price returns to the far side of the box before the target), track whether it then
//        reaches the target on the OTHER side; marked on the chart, counted in the table, with an alert
//  v1.0  First version
//
// Finds CONSOLIDATION BOXES (tight sideways ranges) and names each one by how price came in and how it left.
//  1. Box:      the last N bars fit inside a range no taller than X × ATR (ATR measured just before those bars, so a
//               quiet range is judged against the volatility that came before it). The box then stays open — and can
//               stretch for wicks while it stays under the height limit — until a bar CLOSES outside it.
//  2. Before:   price is compared with where it was a set number of bars before the box began:
//               "after a decline", "after an advance", or neither.
//  3. Name (set when the box breaks):
//               Accumulation      decline  → box → breaks UP     (reversal up)
//               Re-accumulation   advance  → box → breaks UP     (pause, then continuation up)
//               Distribution      advance  → box → breaks DOWN   (reversal down)
//               Re-distribution   decline  → box → breaks DOWN   (pause, then continuation down)
//               With no clear move before the box: up-break = Accumulation, down-break = Distribution.
//     While a box is still open it is labelled "Consolidation" with the side it leans to.
//  4. Volume lean: share of the box's volume that traded on up-closing bars (above 50% = more buying).
//  5. Table:    the open box, plus how often each kind of break went on to travel one box-height beyond the edge
//               before coming back to the far side of the box.
//  6. Head fake: a break that comes back to the far side of the box before reaching its target. From there the
//               script tracks the opposite target (one box-height beyond the far edge) and counts how often price
//               reaches it before returning to the edge it first broke.
//  7. Squeeze Play (the other detection method): a box opens when the Bollinger Bands move inside the Keltner
//               Channel and grows to cover every candle while they stay inside. When the bands move back outside,
//               the squeeze has FIRED: the box is closed and named, and a "Squeeze Fired" panel is shown under it.
//               The direction is the side of the box the firing candle closed beyond (or the half it closed in).
//  8. Squeeze Play, higher timeframe: the same squeeze is read on one higher timeframe (closed candles only). While
//               it is on, a larger box is drawn on this chart. When it fires, the script records whether this
//               chart's own squeeze fired first during it, and whether that smaller fire pointed the same way.
// Nothing repaints: a box is drawn when its Nth bar closes, and named when the breakout bar closes.
indicator("Box Finder – Accumulation / Distribution v1.6", shorttitle = "Box Finder v1.6", overlay = true,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ───────────────────────────── Inputs ─────────────────────────────
grpM = "Detection method"
method   = input.string("Tight range", "Find boxes by", options = ["Tight range", "Squeeze Play"], group = grpM,
     tooltip = "Tight range: the last N bars fit inside a range no taller than X × ATR (settings in the Box group).\nSqueeze Play: the Bollinger Bands are inside the Keltner Channel; the box covers every candle while that lasts.")
sqLen    = input.int(20, "Squeeze Play: length", minval = 2, group = grpM)
sqBB     = input.float(2.0, "Squeeze Play: Bollinger Bands width (standard deviations)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpM)
sqKC     = input.float(1.5, "Squeeze Play: Keltner Channel width (× average true range)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpM,
     tooltip = "1.5 is the classic squeeze. 2.0 catches looser squeezes, 1.0 only the tightest.")
sqMin    = input.int(3, "Squeeze Play: ignore squeezes shorter than (bars)", minval = 1, group = grpM)
sqAlert  = input.bool(true, "Squeeze Play: alert when a squeeze fires", group = grpM)

grpH = "Squeeze Play: higher timeframe"
mtfOn    = input.bool(true, "Track a higher-timeframe squeeze (needs 'Find boxes by' = Squeeze Play)", group = grpH)
mtfTF    = input.timeframe("240", "Higher timeframe", group = grpH)
mtfBox   = input.bool(true, "Draw the higher-timeframe squeeze box on this chart", group = grpH)
mtfCol   = input.color(color.new(color.fuchsia, 0), "Its colour", group = grpH)
mtfTbl   = input.bool(true, "Show the 'little fires before big' table", group = grpH)
mtfPosIn = input.string("Bottom left", "Table position", options = ["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Middle right", "Middle left"], group = grpH)
mtfAlert = input.bool(true, "Alert when the higher-timeframe squeeze fires", group = grpH)

grpB = "Box (Tight range)"
minLen   = input.int(20, "Min box length (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 300, group = grpB,
     tooltip = "A box needs at least this many bars inside the height limit.")
maxH     = input.float(4.0, "Max box height (× ATR)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = grpB,
     tooltip = "Smaller = only very tight ranges. Larger = looser, more boxes.")
atrLen   = input.int(50, "ATR length", minval = 5, group = grpB)
stretch  = input.bool(true, "Let the box stretch for wicks (within the height limit)", group = grpB)
maxLen   = input.int(0, "Max box length (bars, 0 = no limit)", minval = 0, group = grpB,
     tooltip = "A box open longer than this is closed without a name.")

grpP = "Before the box"
lookback = input.int(30, "Compare with the price this many bars before the box", minval = 1, maxval = 400, group = grpP)
priorMin = input.float(3.0, "Counts as a decline / advance from (× ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpP)

grpO = "After the break"
extBars  = input.int(30, "Extend the box edges to the right (bars, 0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 400, group = grpO,
     tooltip = "The old edges often get retested.")
tgtMult  = input.float(1.0, "Target = box heights beyond the edge", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = grpO)
showTgt  = input.bool(true, "Draw the target line", group = grpO)
showFake = input.bool(true, "Mark head fakes and draw the opposite target", group = grpO)

grpV = "Visuals"
colForm = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 0), "Consolidation", group = grpV, inline = "c0")
colAcc  = input.color(color.new(color.lime, 0), "Accumulation", group = grpV, inline = "c1")
colRea  = input.color(color.new(color.teal, 0), "Re-accumulation", group = grpV, inline = "c1")
colDis  = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0), "Distribution", group = grpV, inline = "c2")
colRed  = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 0), "Re-distribution", group = grpV, inline = "c2")
fillT   = input.int(85, "Box fill transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpV)
showMid = input.bool(true, "Draw the box midline", group = grpV)
showLbl = input.bool(true, "Label boxes", group = grpV)
lblSizeIn = input.string("Normal", "Label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group = grpV)
showTbl = input.bool(true, "Show the table", group = grpV)
tblPosIn  = input.string("Top right", "Table position", options = ["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Middle right"], group = grpV)
tblSizeIn = input.string("Small", "Table text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpV)
lblSize = switch lblSizeIn
    "Tiny"  => size.tiny
    "Small" => size.small
    "Large" => size.large
    "Huge"  => size.huge
    => size.normal

// ───────────────────────────── State ─────────────────────────────
atrV = ta.atr(atrLen)
hh   = ta.highest(high, minLen)
ll   = ta.lowest(low, minLen)

// Squeeze Play: Bollinger Bands inside the Keltner Channel
sqBasis = ta.sma(close, sqLen)
sqDev   = sqBB * ta.stdev(close, sqLen)
sqRng   = ta.sma(ta.tr(true), sqLen)
bool sqOn  = sqBasis + sqDev < sqBasis + sqKC * sqRng and sqBasis - sqDev > sqBasis - sqKC * sqRng
bool isSq  = method == "Squeeze Play"

var bool  inBox    = false
var float top      = na
var float bot      = na
var float atr0     = na
var int   startBar = na
var int   lastEnd  = -1
var int   prior    = 0        // 1 = after an advance, -1 = after a decline, 0 = neither
var float upVol    = 0.0
var float dnVol    = 0.0
var box   bx       = na
var line  midLn    = na
var label lb       = na

// results: 0 Accumulation, 1 Re-accumulation, 2 Distribution, 3 Re-distribution
var array<int> nBox  = array.new<int>(4, 0)
var array<int> nDone = array.new<int>(4, 0)
var array<int> nHit  = array.new<int>(4, 0)
var array<int>   pCat  = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   pDir  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> pTgt  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> pFail = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   pStage = array.new<int>()      // 1 = first break, 2 = after a head fake (other side vs first-broken edge), 3 = after a head fake (original vs opposite target)
var array<float> pTop   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> pBot   = array.new<float>()
var array<int> nF2Done = array.new<int>(4, 0)   // head fakes whose second leg is decided
var array<int> nF2Hit  = array.new<int>(4, 0)   // ...and reached the opposite target
var array<int> nF3Done = array.new<int>(4, 0)   // head fakes decided between the original and the opposite target
var array<int> nF3Hit  = array.new<int>(4, 0)   // ...and the original target came first
var int nBoxes = 0

catName(int c) => c == 0 ? "Accumulation" : c == 1 ? "Re-accumulation" : c == 2 ? "Distribution" : "Re-distribution"
catCol(int c)  => c == 0 ? colAcc : c == 1 ? colRea : c == 2 ? colDis : colRed
priorTxt(int p) => p == 1 ? "after an advance" : p == -1 ? "after a decline" : "no clear move before"
leanPct() => upVol + dnVol > 0 ? upVol / (upVol + dnVol) * 100.0 : 50.0

// 1) follow earlier breakouts: target first, or back to the far side of the box first (head fake)?
//    after a head fake: opposite target first, or back to the edge that was first broken?
bool   fakeNow = false
int    fakeDir = 0
if array.size(pCat) > 0
    for i = array.size(pCat) - 1 to 0
        int   d   = array.get(pDir, i)
        float tg  = array.get(pTgt, i)
        float fl  = array.get(pFail, i)
        int   c   = array.get(pCat, i)
        int   stg = array.get(pStage, i)
        bool failed = d == 1 ? low <= fl : high >= fl
        bool hit    = d == 1 ? high >= tg : low <= tg
        if failed or hit
            bool done = true
            if stg == 1
                array.set(nDone, c, array.get(nDone, c) + 1)
                if hit and not failed
                    array.set(nHit, c, array.get(nHit, c) + 1)
                else                                        // head fake: now watch the other side
                    float bt = array.get(pTop, i)
                    float bb = array.get(pBot, i)
                    float t2 = d == 1 ? bb - tgtMult * (bt - bb) : bt + tgtMult * (bt - bb)
                    array.set(pStage, i, 2)
                    array.set(pDir, i, -d)
                    array.set(pTgt, i, t2)
                    array.set(pFail, i, d == 1 ? bt : bb)
                    array.push(pCat, c)                     // second watcher: original target vs opposite target
                    array.push(pDir, d)
                    array.push(pTgt, tg)
                    array.push(pFail, t2)
                    array.push(pStage, 3)
                    array.push(pTop, bt)
                    array.push(pBot, bb)
                    done    := false
                    fakeNow := true
                    fakeDir := -d
                    if showFake
                        color fc = d == 1 ? colDis : colAcc
                        label.new(bar_index, fl, "Head fake " + (d == 1 ? "↑" : "↓") + " (" + catName(c) + ")\nnow watching " + str.tostring(t2, format.mintick),
                             style = d == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(fc, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize)
                        line.new(bar_index, t2, bar_index + math.max(extBars, 10), t2, color = fc, style = line.style_dashed)
            else if stg == 2
                array.set(nF2Done, c, array.get(nF2Done, c) + 1)
                if hit and not failed
                    array.set(nF2Hit, c, array.get(nF2Hit, c) + 1)
            else
                array.set(nF3Done, c, array.get(nF3Done, c) + 1)
                if hit and not failed
                    array.set(nF3Hit, c, array.get(nF3Hit, c) + 1)
            if done
                array.remove(pCat, i)
                array.remove(pDir, i)
                array.remove(pTgt, i)
                array.remove(pFail, i)
                array.remove(pStage, i)
                array.remove(pTop, i)
                array.remove(pBot, i)

// 2) the open box
bool newBox   = false
bool brokeUp  = false
bool brokeDn  = false
int  brokeCat = na
bool sqFired = false
if inBox and isSq and not sqOn and bar_index - startBar < sqMin        // too short to count: drop it
    box.delete(bx)
    line.delete(midLn)
    label.delete(lb)
    lb      := na
    inBox   := false
    lastEnd := bar_index
    nBoxes  -= 1
if inBox
    if isSq ? not sqOn : (close > top or close < bot)
        int d = close > top ? 1 : close < bot ? -1 : close >= (top + bot) / 2 ? 1 : -1
        sqFired := isSq
        int c = d == 1 ? (prior == 1 ? 1 : 0) : (prior == -1 ? 3 : 2)
        float ht = top - bot
        brokeUp  := d == 1
        brokeDn  := d == -1
        brokeCat := c
        array.set(nBox, c, array.get(nBox, c) + 1)
        array.push(pCat, c)
        array.push(pDir, d)
        array.push(pTgt, d == 1 ? top + tgtMult * ht : bot - tgtMult * ht)
        array.push(pFail, d == 1 ? bot : top)
        array.push(pStage, 1)
        array.push(pTop, top)
        array.push(pBot, bot)
        color cc = catCol(c)
        box.set_right(bx, bar_index)
        box.set_border_color(bx, cc)
        box.set_bgcolor(bx, color.new(cc, fillT))
        if not na(midLn)
            line.set_x2(midLn, bar_index)
            line.set_color(midLn, color.new(cc, 40))
        if not na(lb)
            label.delete(lb)
        if showLbl
            label.new(math.round((startBar + bar_index) / 2), bot, (isSq ? "SQUEEZE FIRED " + (d == 1 ? "↑" : "↓") + "\n" + catName(c) + " · range " + str.tostring((top - bot) / bot * 100.0, "#.##") + "%" : catName(c) + (d == 1 ? " ↑" : " ↓")) + "\n" + str.tostring(bar_index - startBar) + " bars · buying " + str.tostring(leanPct(), "#") + "%",
                 style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(cc, 15), textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize)
        if extBars > 0
            line.new(bar_index, top, bar_index + extBars, top, color = color.new(cc, 30), style = line.style_dotted)
            line.new(bar_index, bot, bar_index + extBars, bot, color = color.new(cc, 30), style = line.style_dotted)
        if showTgt
            float tg = d == 1 ? top + tgtMult * ht : bot - tgtMult * ht
            line.new(bar_index, tg, bar_index + math.max(extBars, 10), tg, color = color.new(cc, 0), style = line.style_dashed)
        inBox   := false
        lastEnd := bar_index
    else if maxLen > 0 and bar_index - startBar >= maxLen
        if not na(lb)
            label.delete(lb)
        inBox   := false
        lastEnd := bar_index
    else
        if stretch or isSq
            float nt = math.max(top, high)
            float nb = math.min(bot, low)
            if isSq or nt - nb <= maxH * atr0
                top := nt
                bot := nb
                box.set_top(bx, top)
                box.set_bottom(bx, bot)
                if not na(midLn)
                    line.set_y1(midLn, (top + bot) / 2)
                    line.set_y2(midLn, (top + bot) / 2)
        if close >= open
            upVol += nz(volume)
        else
            dnVol += nz(volume)
        box.set_right(bx, bar_index)
        if not na(midLn)
            line.set_x2(midLn, bar_index)

// 3) look for a new box
if isSq and not inBox and sqOn and bar_index > lastEnd and bar_index > lookback and not na(atrV)
    inBox    := true
    newBox   := true
    top      := high
    bot      := low
    atr0     := atrV
    startBar := bar_index
    nBoxes   += 1
    float mdp0 = (high + low) / 2
    prior := mdp0 - close[lookback] >= priorMin * atrV ? 1 : close[lookback] - mdp0 >= priorMin * atrV ? -1 : 0
    upVol := close >= open ? nz(volume) : 0.0
    dnVol := close >= open ? 0.0 : nz(volume)
    bx := box.new(bar_index, top, bar_index, bot, border_color = colForm, bgcolor = color.new(colForm, fillT), border_width = 1)
    midLn := showMid ? line.new(bar_index, mdp0, bar_index, mdp0, color = color.new(colForm, 40), style = line.style_dotted) : na
    lb := na
if not isSq and not inBox and not brokeUp and not brokeDn
    float a0 = atrV[minLen]
    int   st = bar_index - minLen + 1
    if not na(a0) and a0 > 0 and st > lastEnd and bar_index >= minLen + lookback and hh - ll <= maxH * a0 and close <= hh and close >= ll
        inBox    := true
        newBox   := true
        top      := hh
        bot      := ll
        atr0     := a0
        startBar := st
        nBoxes   += 1
        float ref = close[minLen - 1 + lookback]
        float mdp = (hh + ll) / 2
        prior := mdp - ref >= priorMin * a0 ? 1 : ref - mdp >= priorMin * a0 ? -1 : 0
        upVol := 0.0
        dnVol := 0.0
        for k = 0 to minLen - 1
            if close[k] >= open[k]
                upVol += nz(volume[k])
            else
                dnVol += nz(volume[k])
        bx := box.new(st, top, bar_index, bot, border_color = colForm, bgcolor = color.new(colForm, fillT), border_width = 1)
        midLn := showMid ? line.new(st, mdp, bar_index, mdp, color = color.new(colForm, 40), style = line.style_dotted) : na
        lb := na

// label of the open box (kept up to date)
if inBox and showLbl
    string lean = prior == -1 ? "possible accumulation" : prior == 1 ? "possible distribution" : "direction open"
    string txt  = (isSq ? "Squeeze on · " + str.tostring(bar_index - startBar + 1) + " bars · " : "Consolidation · ") + priorTxt(prior) + "\n" + lean + " · buying " + str.tostring(leanPct(), "#") + "%"
    if na(lb)
        lb := label.new(math.round((startBar + bar_index) / 2), bot, txt, style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(colForm, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize)
    else
        label.set_text(lb, txt)
        label.set_xy(lb, math.round((startBar + bar_index) / 2), bot)

// ───────────────────────────── Squeeze Play: higher timeframe ─────────────────────────────
// squeeze state on whatever timeframe this runs in: [on, fired this candle, direction of the fire]
sqHtf() =>
    float b  = ta.sma(close, sqLen)
    float dv = sqBB * ta.stdev(close, sqLen)
    float r  = ta.sma(ta.tr(true), sqLen)
    bool  on = b + dv < b + sqKC * r and b - dv > b - sqKC * r
    var float t  = na
    var float bo = na
    var int   n  = 0
    bool fired = false
    int  dir   = 0
    if on
        t  := n == 0 ? high : math.max(t, high)
        bo := n == 0 ? low : math.min(bo, low)
        n  += 1
    else
        if n >= sqMin
            fired := true
            dir   := close > t ? 1 : close < bo ? -1 : close >= (t + bo) / 2 ? 1 : -1
        n := 0
    [on, fired, dir]
sqHtfClosed() =>
    [a, f, d] = sqHtf()
    [a[1], f[1], d[1]]
[hOn, hFired, hDir] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, mtfTF, sqHtfClosed(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
tfLabel(string tf) =>
    int sec = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    sec >= 604800 and sec % 604800 == 0 ? str.tostring(sec / 604800) + "W" : sec >= 86400 and sec % 86400 == 0 ? str.tostring(sec / 86400) + "D" : sec >= 3600 and sec % 3600 == 0 ? str.tostring(sec / 3600) + "h" : str.tostring(sec / 60) + "m"

var bool  wOn       = false       // a higher-timeframe squeeze is in progress
var int   wStart    = na
var float wTop      = na
var float wBot      = na
var int   wFires    = 0           // this chart's squeeze fires inside it
var int   wFirstDir = 0
var int   wLastDir  = 0
var int   wLastBar  = na
var box   wBox      = na
var label wLb       = na
var int hTot       = 0            // higher-timeframe squeezes that fired
var int hWithLittle = 0           // …with at least one fire on this chart first
var int hFirstSame = 0            // …whose FIRST small fire pointed the same way as the big one
var int hLastSame  = 0            // …whose LAST small fire pointed the same way
var int hFiresSum  = 0
var int hLeadSum   = 0            // bars between the last small fire and the big fire
bool bigFired = false
bool mtfLive  = mtfOn and isSq
bool hNew     = timeframe.change(mtfTF)

if mtfLive
    // 1) the big squeeze has fired (known on the first chart bar after its candle closed)
    if wOn and hNew and hFired
        bigFired := true
        hTot += 1
        if wFires > 0
            hWithLittle += 1
            hFiresSum   += wFires
            hLeadSum    += bar_index - wLastBar
            if wFirstDir == hDir
                hFirstSame += 1
            if wLastDir == hDir
                hLastSame += 1
        color fc = hDir == 1 ? color.lime : color.red
        if not na(wBox)
            box.set_right(wBox, bar_index)
            box.set_border_color(wBox, fc)
        if not na(wLb)
            label.set_xy(wLb, math.round((wStart + bar_index) / 2), wBot)
            label.set_text(wLb, tfLabel(mtfTF) + " SQUEEZE FIRED " + (hDir == 1 ? "↑" : "↓") + "\n" + (wFires > 0 ? tfLabel(timeframe.period) + " fired first: " + str.tostring(wFires) + "×, last " +
                 (wLastDir == 1 ? "↑" : "↓") + " " + str.tostring(bar_index - wLastBar) + " bars earlier" + (wLastDir == hDir ? " (same way)" : " (other way)") : tfLabel(timeframe.period) + " did not fire first"))
            label.set_color(wLb, color.new(fc, 15))
        wOn  := false
        wBox := na
        wLb  := na
    else if wOn and not hOn                                  // ended without counting (too short)
        box.delete(wBox)
        label.delete(wLb)
        wOn  := false
        wBox := na
        wLb  := na
    // 2) a big squeeze starts
    if not wOn and hOn and not (hNew and hFired)
        wOn       := true
        wStart    := bar_index
        wTop      := high
        wBot      := low
        wFires    := 0
        wFirstDir := 0
        wLastDir  := 0
        wLastBar  := na
        if mtfBox
            wBox := box.new(bar_index, wTop, bar_index, wBot, border_color = mtfCol, border_width = 2, bgcolor = color.new(mtfCol, 94))
            wLb  := showLbl ? label.new(bar_index, wBot, tfLabel(mtfTF) + " squeeze on", style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(mtfCol, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize) : na
    // 3) while it lasts: grow the box, and note this chart's own fires
    if wOn
        wTop := math.max(wTop, high)
        wBot := math.min(wBot, low)
        if not na(wBox)
            box.set_top(wBox, wTop)
            box.set_bottom(wBox, wBot)
            box.set_right(wBox, bar_index)
        if sqFired
            wFires += 1
            wLastDir := brokeUp ? 1 : -1
            wLastBar := bar_index
            if wFirstDir == 0
                wFirstDir := wLastDir
        if not na(wLb)
            label.set_xy(wLb, math.round((wStart + bar_index) / 2), wBot)
            label.set_text(wLb, tfLabel(mtfTF) + " squeeze on · " + tfLabel(timeframe.period) + " fired " + str.tostring(wFires) + "× so far" + (wFires > 0 ? ", last " + (wLastDir == 1 ? "↑" : "↓") : ""))
if bigFired and mtfAlert
    alert("Box Finder " + syminfo.ticker + ": " + tfLabel(mtfTF) + " SQUEEZE FIRED " + (hDir == 1 ? "UP" : "DOWN") + (wFires > 0 ? " — the " + tfLabel(timeframe.period) + " squeeze fired first (" +
         (wLastDir == hDir ? "same way" : "other way") + ")" : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

mtfPos = switch mtfPosIn
    "Top left"     => position.top_left
    "Top right"    => position.top_right
    "Bottom right" => position.bottom_right
    "Middle right" => position.middle_right
    "Middle left"  => position.middle_left
    => position.bottom_left
var table mt = table.new(mtfPos, 2, 8, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60), border_width = 1, frame_color = color.gray, frame_width = 1)
mrow(int r, string a, string b, color bc = color.white) =>
    table.cell(mt, 0, r, a, text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(mt, 1, r, b, text_color = bc, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_right)
share(int a, int n) => n > 0 ? str.tostring(a) + " of " + str.tostring(n) + "  (" + str.tostring(a / n * 100.0, "#") + "%)" : "–"
if mtfTbl and barstate.isfirst
    table.merge_cells(mt, 0, 0, 1, 0)
    table.merge_cells(mt, 0, 7, 1, 7)
if mtfTbl and barstate.islast
    string little = tfLabel(timeframe.period)
    string big    = tfLabel(mtfTF)
    table.cell(mt, 0, 0, "Squeeze Play — does " + little + " fire before " + big + "?", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 40))
    if not isSq
        table.cell(mt, 0, 7, "Set 'Find boxes by' to Squeeze Play to use this.", text_color = color.orange, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    else
        mrow(1, big + " squeezes that fired", str.tostring(hTot))
        mrow(2, little + " fired first, during the " + big + " squeeze", share(hWithLittle, hTot))
        mrow(3, "…average number of " + little + " fires", hWithLittle > 0 ? str.tostring(hFiresSum / hWithLittle, "#.#") : "–")
        mrow(4, "…first " + little + " fire pointed the same way as " + big, share(hFirstSame, hWithLittle), hWithLittle > 0 and hFirstSame / hWithLittle > 0.55 ? color.lime : color.white)
        mrow(5, "…last " + little + " fire pointed the same way as " + big, share(hLastSame, hWithLittle), hWithLittle > 0 and hLastSame / hWithLittle > 0.55 ? color.lime : color.white)
        mrow(6, "…last " + little + " fire came, on average", hWithLittle > 0 ? str.tostring(hLeadSum / hWithLittle, "#") + " bars before" : "–")
        table.cell(mt, 0, 7, "Now: " + big + (wOn ? " squeeze ON · " + little + " has fired " + str.tostring(wFires) + "× in it" + (wFires > 0 ? ", last " + (wLastDir == 1 ? "↑" : "↓") : "") : " not in a squeeze") +
             "  ·  50% same-way = no information", text_color = wOn ? color.yellow : color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)

// ───────────────────────────── Alerts ─────────────────────────────
if newBox
    alert("Box Finder " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + ": new consolidation box " + str.tostring(bot, format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(top, format.mintick) +
         " (" + priorTxt(prior) + ")", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if brokeUp or brokeDn
    alert("Box Finder " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + ": " + catName(brokeCat) + (brokeUp ? " — broke UP through " + str.tostring(top, format.mintick) : " — broke DOWN through " + str.tostring(bot, format.mintick)),
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if sqFired and sqAlert
    alert("Box Finder " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + ": SQUEEZE FIRED " + (brokeUp ? "UP" : "DOWN") + " — box " + str.tostring(bot, format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(top, format.mintick),
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if fakeNow
    alert("Box Finder " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + ": HEAD FAKE — the break failed, now watching the " + (fakeDir == 1 ? "upside" : "downside") + " target", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plotshape(brokeUp, "Box broke up", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.lime, size = size.small)
plotshape(brokeDn, "Box broke down", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.red, size = size.small)

// ───────────────────────────── Table ─────────────────────────────
tblPos = switch tblPosIn
    "Top left"     => position.top_left
    "Bottom right" => position.bottom_right
    "Bottom left"  => position.bottom_left
    "Middle right" => position.middle_right
    => position.top_right
tblSize = switch tblSizeIn
    "Tiny"   => size.tiny
    "Normal" => size.normal
    "Large"  => size.large
    => size.small
var table tbl = table.new(tblPos, 6, 12, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60), border_width = 1,
     frame_color = color.gray, frame_width = 1)
cell(int c, int r, string txt, color tc = color.white) =>
    table.cell(tbl, c, r, txt, text_color = tc, text_size = tblSize, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)

if showTbl and barstate.isfirst
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 0, 5, 0)
    for r = 1 to 5
        table.merge_cells(tbl, 1, r, 5, r)
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 11, 5, 11)
if showTbl and barstate.islast
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, "Box Finder v1.6 — " + (isSq ? "Squeeze Play (BB " + str.tostring(sqBB, "#.#") + " inside KC " + str.tostring(sqKC, "#.#") + ")" : str.tostring(minLen) + "+ bars within " + str.tostring(maxH, "#.##") + " × ATR"), text_color = color.white, text_size = tblSize,
         bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 40))
    cell(0, 1, "Now", color.silver)
    cell(1, 1, inBox ? (isSq ? "Squeeze on · " : "In a box · ") + priorTxt(prior) : (isSq ? "No squeeze" : "No box"), inBox ? color.yellow : color.white)
    cell(0, 2, "Top / bottom", color.silver)
    cell(1, 2, inBox ? str.tostring(top, format.mintick) + " / " + str.tostring(bot, format.mintick) : "–")
    cell(0, 3, "Height · length", color.silver)
    cell(1, 3, inBox ? str.tostring((top - bot) / bot * 100.0, "#.##") + "% · " + str.tostring(bar_index - startBar + 1) + " bars" : "–")
    cell(0, 4, "Volume on up bars", color.silver)
    cell(1, 4, inBox ? str.tostring(leanPct(), "#") + "%" : "–", inBox ? (leanPct() > 55 ? color.lime : leanPct() < 45 ? color.red : color.white) : color.white)
    cell(0, 5, "Boxes found", color.silver)
    cell(1, 5, str.tostring(nBoxes))
    cell(0, 6, "Break type", color.silver)
    cell(1, 6, "Count", color.silver)
    cell(2, 6, "Reached\ntarget", color.silver)
    cell(3, 6, "Head\nfakes", color.silver)
    cell(4, 6, "…then other\ntarget", color.silver)
    cell(5, 6, "…or original\ntarget first", color.silver)
    for c = 0 to 3
        int done = array.get(nDone, c)
        cell(0, 7 + c, catName(c) + (c < 2 ? " ↑" : " ↓"), catCol(c))
        cell(1, 7 + c, str.tostring(array.get(nBox, c)))
        cell(2, 7 + c, done > 0 ? str.tostring(array.get(nHit, c) / done * 100.0, "#") + "% of " + str.tostring(done) : "–")
        int fakes = done - array.get(nHit, c)
        int d2    = array.get(nF2Done, c)
        cell(3, 7 + c, done > 0 ? str.tostring(fakes) + " (" + str.tostring(fakes / done * 100.0, "#") + "%)" : "–")
        int d3 = array.get(nF3Done, c)
        int h3 = array.get(nF3Hit, c)
        cell(5, 7 + c, d3 > 0 ? str.tostring(h3) + " of " + str.tostring(d3) + " (" + str.tostring(h3 / d3 * 100.0, "#") + "%)" : "–", d3 > 0 ? catCol(c) : color.white)
        cell(4, 7 + c, d2 > 0 ? str.tostring(array.get(nF2Hit, c) / d2 * 100.0, "#") + "% of " + str.tostring(d2) : "–", d2 > 0 ? (c < 2 ? colDis : colAcc) : color.white)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 11, "Target: " + str.tostring(tgtMult, "#.##") + " box height past the edge.\nHead fake: back to the far side first.\nNo-edge rate ≈ " +
         str.tostring(100.0 / (1.0 + tgtMult), "#") + "%. Hover for details.", text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left,
         tooltip = "Reached target: price travelled the target distance beyond the broken edge before returning to the far side of the box.\nHead fake: it returned to the far side first.\nThen reached the other target: after a head fake, price travelled the same distance beyond the far edge before getting back to the edge it first broke.\nOr original target first: after a head fake, price reached the ORIGINAL target before the opposite one (no-edge rate ≈ " + str.tostring(tgtMult / (1.0 + 2.0 * tgtMult) * 100.0, "#") + "%, because it is further away).\nNo-edge rate: what a coin flip would give for these distances.")
